From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:28:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] fix(backend): stop only Studio's own orphaned
 publishers; never start untracked ones

- The startup sweep stopped any publisher process of this user whose parent
  was not a Python program, other programs' publishers included, and missed
  ones adopted by a Python subreaper. It now stops only publishers a Studio
  backend recorded, matched by pid and start time, whose backend is gone.
- A camera connects attach-only, then checks the publisher's settings: if the
  publisher Studio started exited in between, the base class no longer starts
  an untracked one of its own.
- Of two setting changes waiting for one camera (a camera form clicked
  through quickly), the newer wins, instead of whichever got the lock last.
- The camera preview reconnects after an error, such as a stalled camera, and
  shows the error until a frame arrives.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
